{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "FDM tensile bars: layer height, material, nozzle temperature and print speed",
  "notes": "ISO 527-2 type 1A tensile bars printed flat (XY, ±45° raster, 3 perimeters) on an enclosed FDM printer with a 0.4 mm nozzle. Nozzle temperature is set as an offset from each material's datasheet value (PLA 210 °C, PETG 240 °C, ABS 250 °C). Spools stay on the printer between prints, so the filament moisture content rises over the campaign; it is measured with a moisture analyser before each print and recorded as an environmental factor. The PETG spool was dried once during the campaign (see run notes). Tensile strength is the mean of three bars per run; dimensional error is the mean absolute deviation of three 20.00 mm reference features printed on the same plate.",
  "factors": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "symbol": "A",
      "name": "Layer height",
      "units": "mm",
      "kind": {
        "type": "discrete",
        "levels": [
          0.1,
          0.15,
          0.2,
          0.3
        ]
      },
      "role": "controlled"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
